    {
        "content": "<p>As I am learning lean, one of the most frustrating experiences is having <code>rw</code> fail with something that looks by the error to be a very reasonable ask for <code>rw</code>. At this point, I have learned enough to dig in and find the underlying mismatch, but I wonder if something in the error reporting can be improved.</p>\n<p>Prompted the most recent failure, I made a MRE </p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">SomeProp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Prop</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">True</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">SomeProp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">↔</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">True</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"gr\">sorry</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Int</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">SomeProp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">rw</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>Again the issue is extremely obvious here, but in real situations there are 4-5 arguments that match and one which doesn't and again the error doesn't help pinpoint which. My problem is that the error emitted is:</p>\n<p><img alt=\"Screenshot 2026-05-08 at 8.59.03 AM.png\" class=\"inline-image\" data-original-content-type=\"image/png\" data-original-dimensions=\"1478x552\" data-original-src=\"/user_uploads/3121/Sj5Y87KWq_g-rYGStZ812YXU/Screenshot-2026-05-08-at-8.59.03AM.png\" src=\"/user_uploads/thumbnail/3121/Sj5Y87KWq_g-rYGStZ812YXU/Screenshot-2026-05-08-at-8.59.03AM.png/840x560.webp\"></p>\n<p>Which I read as <code>SomeProp &lt;free variable&gt;</code> can't be found in the expression <code>Someprop &lt;bound var&gt;</code> which is confusing to me - surely free var can be unified with bound var? More over the error is not clickable in VSCode, so it leaves a new comer in a very odd spot.</p>\n<p>I know by know how to debug this, I make a <code>have := hPNat a</code> and hover and click through the InfoView until I find the mismatched term or type, but again I wonder if the error could be changed to directly say - you are asking me to rewrite a term with type <code>Nat</code> while I have a term with type <code>Int</code>.</p>",
        "id": 593827454,
        "sender_full_name": "Rado Kirov",
        "timestamp": 1778256764
    },
