    {
        "content": "<p><span aria-label=\"mind\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f92f\" role=\"img\" title=\"mind\">:mind:</span> somehow it never crossed my mind to click on the error in the InfoView and I have been just starting at hovers over the red squigglies. Indeed this makes it way easier to debug. I need to update my priors that even if something says <code>?a</code> it can be <code>?a : Int</code> - i.e. the variable is free, but the type is bound, but that is easy to find with a bit of clicking through. </p>\n<p>If someone thinks the static error can be improved too, that can be further discussed, but this is a lot less annoying in vscode now that I know where to look. Thanks!</p>",
