    {
        "content": "<p>In Neovim FWIW it's possible to make the diagnostic hover also be interactive (so lean.nvim does so in the Lean buffer as well):</p>\n<p><img alt=\"Screenshot 2026-05-08 at 13.51.31.png\" class=\"inline-image\" data-original-content-type=\"image/png\" data-original-dimensions=\"829x298\" data-original-src=\"/user_uploads/3121/x0kp6jcccKA2u_AwIrLsm7R_/Screenshot-2026-05-08-at-13.51.31.png\" src=\"/user_uploads/thumbnail/3121/x0kp6jcccKA2u_AwIrLsm7R_/Screenshot-2026-05-08-at-13.51.31.png/840x560.webp\"></p>\n<p>But my life is a bit easier than Marc's there I think on editor extensibility.</p>",
